1
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:06,729
Aomi works across EVM and Solana without

2
00:00:06,769 --> 00:00:10,416
making the user switch networks between steps.

3
00:00:12,068 --> 00:00:15,105
This single request combines a Base lending position,

4
00:00:15,145 --> 00:00:19,245
a bridge to Arbitrum, and a Solana liquid-staking route.

5
00:00:19,695 --> 00:00:23,858
Aomi activates five protocol skills, checks both wallets,

6
00:00:23,898 --> 00:00:27,847
and builds each leg on the chain where it belongs.

7
00:00:28,297 --> 00:00:30,475
On Base, an ordered four-transaction

8
00:00:30,515 --> 00:00:31,961
simulation supplies four

9
00:00:32,001 --> 00:00:34,584
USDC to Aave and routes another

10
00:00:34,624 --> 00:00:37,192
four through Across to Arbitrum.

11
00:00:37,642 --> 00:00:43,767
The bridge quote returns 3.992124 USDC on Arbitrum.

12
00:00:43,807 --> 00:00:45,137
Delivery is not claimed;

13
00:00:45,177 --> 00:00:48,952
the quote and source-chain calls are what were simulated.

14
00:00:49,402 --> 00:00:54,459
On Solana, account creation and a 0.05 SOL Marinade

15
00:00:54,499 --> 00:00:58,158
stake pass together in one atomic simulation.

16
00:00:58,608 --> 00:01:01,714
The Kamino leg is withheld because the simulator cannot

17
00:01:01,754 --> 00:01:06,939
validate spending newly minted mSOL in that same batch.

18
00:01:06,979 --> 00:01:09,686
Every transaction remains unsigned.

19
00:01:10,136 --> 00:01:12,464
One orchestration layer, multiple chains,

20
00:01:12,504 --> 00:01:16,616
and simulation as the gate before wallet authority.
